Source: secubox-threat-analyst
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Gerald KERMA <devel@cybermind.fr>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2

Package: secubox-threat-analyst
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, secubox-core (>= 1.0.0)
Description: SecuBox Threat Analyst — AI agent that writes detection scenarios
 AI-assisted threat analysis: ingests recent alerts, proposes new
 detection scenarios, and writes them under /etc/secubox/scenarios/
 for operator review and reload.
 .
 Distinct from sibling packages in the threats cluster:
  - secubox-threats — umbrella dashboard aggregating
    Suricata + WAF alerts (read-only).
  - secubox-cve-triage — CVE vulnerability triage workflow.
  - secubox-network-anomaly — DNS-log anomaly detection.
  - secubox-cyberfeed — threat-intel feed aggregator.
  - secubox-ipblock — nftables-driven IP blocklist enforcement.
  - secubox-openclaw — OSINT / domain reconnaissance.
